  "question": {
    "text": "The letters of the word &#39;MANKIND&#39; are written in all possible orders and arranged in serial order as in an English dictionary. Then the serial number of the word &#39;MANKIND&#39; is _____ ."
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "1492",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"1\" cellspacing=\"1\" style=\"width: 100px;\">\t<tbody>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi></math></td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math></td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math></td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math></td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></math></td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math></td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi></math></td>\t\t</tr>\t</tbody></table><p>Arranging the letters alphabetically, we get</p><p>ADIKMNN</p><p>When the word starts with any of the letters A/D/I/K, the number of possibilities<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo>!</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>1440</mn></math></p><p>Now when the word starts with MA, then the number of possibilities<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>!</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>36</mn></math></p><p>Now when the word starts with MAN, then the number of possibilities<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>!</mo><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>12</mn></math></p><p>Now when the word starts with MANK, then the number of possibilities<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math></p><p>Hence, rank of the work MANKIND is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1492</mn></math></p></blockquote>"
  }
